The gnome wields a scroll named Spoilers! -more-















Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 10-Mar-93 Various and sundry by
Michael Jason Lewis@lela 
> Frightening message:  "The gnome wields a sword named Vorpal Blade!"  Good
> thing gnomes are such wimps.

No doubt.  Nothing quite like the feeling you get when you realize that
something is coming at you with a sword that can kill you in one blow (I
got this exact message myself, once).

> Strange, though--I didn't get a jolt when I wielded it.  Just lucky, I guess.
> I did "miss wildly" occasionally, though.

The "miss wildly" comes when you are attacking something that lacks a
head, and Vorpal Blade gets a critical hit (i.e., the creature would
have died if it had a head, but it didn't, so you "missed wildly"). 
However, in 3.1.0 (I don't have 3.1.1 yet so this might have been
fixed), you don't really miss wildly, since I've killed things when I
"missed wildly" as well as causing other stuff like black puddings to
divide (which I think is really obnoxious...if I missed wildly, let me
miss).

> Why did I get the message "Your pack shakes violently!"?  I didn't have any
> eggs that would have hatched...

Magic trap, probably.  This is one of those nonsense messages that magic
traps pipe up with occasionally, along with stuff like the yearning for
your distant homeland and the smelling of charred flesh.  No biggie.

> Does #dipping daggers into a potion of sickness help any?

I don't remember if it does in 3.1 or not.  I seem to recall "no", but I
might be wrong here.

